# Machine stage-reports that /pharn-dev-regress and /pharn-dev-verify must write VERBATIM — each is its
# floor helper's stdout JSON, deliberately NOT formatted so the recorded verdict is the helper's own
# bytes. Without these entries those two requirements conflict with whole-repo `format:check`, which the
# SAME commands run as a verdict-owning gate — but only when an array is non-empty: `JSON.stringify(…,
# null, 2)` expands `"failing_gates": ["test"]` across three lines where prettier wants it inline. Every
# run that reached those steps with a PASS had `[]`, on which the two agree, so the conflict sat latent
# until the first FAIL — at which point the stage's own artifact reddened the gate the stage owns.
# The product twins are listed too: same requirement, same latency, and no reason to wait for the first
# product-pipeline FAIL to discover it.
.dev/features/*/verify-report.json
.dev/features/*/regression-report.json
pharn/features/*/verify-report.json
pharn/features/*/regression-report.json

